        "id": 96027,
        "name": "Sefirit",
        "username": "Sefirit",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/s/e68b1a/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2014-06-17T15:39:33.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Silverleaf\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/silverleaf/48/2332_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Silverleaf:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>No, really. How is the tier thing useful? Do people think, \"Oh I fancy a challenge today, I'll pick a low-tier hero\"? I'm curious since I don't tier and almost exclusively randomise everything.&nbsp;</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>And I failed to mention this earlier, but to some degree yes.&nbsp; My group mostly refuses to play Legacy in any incarnation as well as Team Leader Tachyon and Dark Visionary because they proved to be way too potent.&nbsp; Teirs are not just about which heroes are weaker, but which ones are very strong as well.&nbsp; We randomize for the most part, but Legacy is removed from the list and if Tachyon comes up we only play the base version.</p>",
        "post_number": 74,
